METIS (CeCILL-C) — NOT A SOURCE; BENCHMARK ONLY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Until 2026-09-24 the fast neutral-beam model, the minority-ICRH chain and the
fast-wave and EC current-drive efficiencies were transcriptions of METIS (CEA/
IRFM, CeCILL-C).  They were REMOVED and rewritten from the published literature
in a clean room: the specification was written from the papers alone, and the
implementer saw neither METIS nor the removed code.  The rewrite lives in
rust/fylite/src/hcd/, each function citing the paper and equation it implements
(Janev, Boley & Post 1989; Riviere 1971; Hill et al. 2023; Stix 1972 and 1975;
Mikkelsen & Singer 1983; Lin-Liu & Hinton 1997; Lin-Liu, Chan & Prater 2003;
Eriksson & Hellsten 1995; Mandrekas 1992; the ITER Physics Design Guidelines
1989; Wesson, Tokamaks).
No METIS code, and no transcription of it, is in this distribution.

METIS results are still used as a BENCHMARK: numbers from its published
certification runs are compared against this distribution's answers in the test
suite and the benchmark register.  Those are comparisons with another code's
output, credited in ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS; they are not a source of this code.

★RABBIT is named in nbi.py as the FIDELITY TIER the beam model belongs to
(Weiland et al., Nucl. Fusion 58 (2018) 082032), not as a source: RABBIT's own
source is MPCDF-licensed and is not obtainable, so nothing here derives from it.

