DERIVED WORK — EPEDNN.jl (Apache-2.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The H-mode pedestal surrogate is a TRANSCRIPTION of EPEDNN.jl's evaluation, and
the numbers it evaluates are that model's own weights.

    Upstream:  ProjectTorreyPines/EPEDNN.jl,
               https://github.com/ProjectTorreyPines/EPEDNN.jl
               model `delta_ne_sqrt_power` in `data/EPED1NNmodel.bson`
    Terms:     Apache License 2.0 (a copy travels at
               rust/tools/data/EPEDNN-LICENSE, beside the BSON it applies to)
    Authors:   O. Meneghini / General Atomics and the EPEDNN.jl contributors

Files in this distribution that derive from it:

    rust/fylite/src/pedestal.rs        <- EPEDNN.jl::pedestal_array, line for
                                          line: the ten inputs and their order,
                                          `delta += 1` and the absolute values,
                                          the per-output power law, the MLP
                                          correction with its scaling, plus
                                          ::extrapolation_distance and
                                          ::effective_triangularity
    rust/fylite/src/pedestal_tables.rs <- the model's numbers, extracted by
                                          rust/tools/extract_epednn.py from the
                                          vendored BSON (a 10->32->32->32->18
                                          GELU MLP and the power-law
                                          coefficients); the sha256 of the copy
                                          is stamped into the generated header
                                          and re-checked by the extractor

STATEMENT OF CHANGES.  Julia to Rust; the weights are generated into the source
rather than read from a BSON at runtime, so the shipped library has no model
file to lose.  The out-of-box behaviour is upstream's and deliberately so —
inputs outside the training box are answered WITH the extrapolation distance
reported rather than refused.  What this port adds is a refusal for a machine
that cannot be normalized at all (non-finite, or a non-positive
size / field / current / density), where upstream would evaluate anyway.

★The model is EPED1-NN (Meneghini et al., Nucl. Fusion 57 (2017) 086034), a
neural-network surrogate of EPED (Snyder et al., Phys. Plasmas 16 (2009)
056118).  The FULL EPED model is a stability-code scan (ELITE); nothing here
derives from it or from ELITE.

